tly re-doing all our existing working UI?\"), and after the explanation **re-confirmed** \"Still the existing project\".\n- **Constraint (verbatim):** \"if the `.design-sync` is going to be commited, make sure it is done in a separate stacked PR on the current one, as per /gh-stack\".\n\n## 2. Key Technical Concepts\n\n- Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, Tailwind CSS v4 (arbitrary properties, `@property`, `inset-ring-*`, `motion-reduce:`, `max-md:`, `group-has-[…]`, `data-[…]` variants), shadcn/ui base-nova primitives, Base UI (`useRender`, `mergeProps`), `cva`, `tailwind-merge` via `cn`.\n- CSS `mask-image` gradients driven by registered `@property` custom properties; `@keyframes` with `both` fill to animate *from* a value a transition cannot reach.\n- Grid-track animation (`grid-template-columns: 0fr → 1fr`) to animate to intrinsic width without knowing pixel sizes.\n- `ResizeObserver`-based measurement written straight to the DOM (no React state) to avoid re-renders across hundreds of rows.\n- Storybook 10 + `nextjs-vite`, Vitest browser-mode play-function tests, `sb.mock` module redirects, storyproof visual baselines.\n- pnpm workspace resolution quirks (virtual store `.pnpm`, no self-linking, `@types/react` not hoisted).\n- esbuild metafile bundle-composition analysis.\n- design-sync converter: `package-build.mjs`, `package-validate.mjs`, `resync.mjs`, `lib/`, `storybook/compare.mjs`; `_ds_bundle.js` IIFE global, `_ds_sync.json` anchor, `titleMap`, `overrides` (`skip`, `cardMode`, `primaryStory`), owned previews in `.design-sync/previews/`.\n- GitHub: `pull_request` workflows do not run on a conflicted PR (no `refs/pull/N/merge` ref) — CI silently produces zero runs.\n- Vivaldi's \"Webpage Focus / Full Keyboard Access → Focus Forms Only\" default skips links in tab order (equivalent to Firefox `accessibility.tabfocus=3`).\n\n## 3. Files and Code Sections\n\n**`apps/web/components/sidebar-row-title.tsx`** (new; the fade + marquee title)\n- Final shape: trailing-edge-only mask, `ResizeObserver` on both clip and text nodes, dev warning when not inside a `SidebarMenuItem`, write-diffing to avoid redundant DOM writes.\n```tsx\nconst SCROLL_SPEED = 60;                       // px/s\nconst SCROLL_MS = { MIN: 150, MAX: 2500 };\nconst SCROLL_DELAY = 300;\n// mask (trailing only):\n\"[mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,#000_calc(100%_-_var(--marquee-fade-r)),transparent_100%)]\",\n\"data-[clipped=true]:[--marquee-fade-r:var(--marquee-fade-max)]\",\n\"[transition:--marquee-fade-r_150ms_ease-out]\",\n\"group-hover/menu-item:data-[clipped=true]:[animation:marquee-tail_150ms_ease-out_var(--marquee-end-ms)_both]\",\n\"motion-reduce:animate-none!\",\n// inner span:\n\"group-hover/menu-item:data-[clipped=true]:translate-x-(--marquee-x) group-hover/menu-item:delay-(--marquee-delay) group-hover/menu-item:duration-(--marquee-ms) group-hover/menu-item:ease-linear\",\n\"motion-reduce:translate-x-0! motion-reduce:transition-none\",\n```\n```tsx\nfunction writeScroll(clip: HTMLElement, shift: number) {\n  const duration = Math.round(Math.min(SCROLL_MS.MAX, Math.max(SCROLL_MS.MIN, (shift / SCROLL_SPEED) * 1000)));\n  clip.style.setProperty(\"--marquee-x\", `${-Math.round(shift)}px`);\n  clip.style.setProperty(\"--marquee-ms\", `${duration}ms`);\n  clip.style.setProperty(\"--marquee-delay\", `${SCROLL_DELAY}ms`);\n  clip.style.setProperty(\"--marquee-end-ms\", `${SCROLL_DELAY + duration}ms`);\n}\n```\n- Props: `text`, `animateChanges`, `shimmer`, `className`. Uses `useTypewriter(text, { enabled: animateChanges })` and applies `shimmer && \"shimmer motion-reduce:animate-none\"` to the inner span.\n\n**`apps/web/components/hover-reveal.tsx`** (new; replaced `sidebar-row-actions.ts`, which was deleted)\n```tsx\nexport function HoverReveal({ atRest = false, className, children }) // grid 0fr→1fr\n  \"grid transition-[grid-template-columns] duration-150 ease-out\",\n  \"group-data-[collapsible=icon]:hidden\",           // added after the collapsed-rail bug\n  atRest ? \"grid-cols-[1fr]\" : [\"grid-cols-[0fr]\",\n    \"group-hover/menu-item:grid-cols-[1fr]\",\n    \"group-focus-within/menu-item:grid-cols-[1fr]\",\n    \"group-has-[[aria-expanded=true]]/menu-item:grid-cols-[1fr]\",\n    \"max-md:grid-cols-[1fr]\"],\n  // inner clip, scoped so it does not eat focus rings:\n  atRest ? \"overflow-visible\" : \"overflow-hidden group-focus-within/menu-item:overflow-visible\"\n\nexport function SidebarRowAction({ className, ...props }: React.ComponentProps<\"button\">)\n  // byte-for-byte the vendored SidebarMenuAction appearance minus positioning:\n  \"relative flex aspect-square w-5 items-center justify-center rounded-md p-0 text-sidebar-foreground ring-sidebar-ring outline-hidden after:absolute after:-inset-2 hover:bg-sidebar-accent hover:text-sidebar-accent-foreground focus-visible:ring-2 md:after:hidden [&>svg]:size-4 [&>svg]:shrink-0\",\n  \"aria-expanded:bg-sidebar-accent aria-expanded:text-sidebar-accent-foreground\",\n  \"ml-1\",\n```\n\n**`apps/web/components/use-typewriter.ts`** (new) — `DELETE = {PER_CHAR_MS:15, TOTAL_MS:350}`, `TYPE = {PER_CHAR_MS:30, TOTAL_MS:1200}`; explicit `phase: \"delete\" | \"type\"` (without it the branches ping-pong forever); reduced-motion via `useSyncExternalStore` + `window.matchMedia` (no motion library — `framer-motion` is declared in apps/web but imported nowhere).\n\n**`apps/web/components/use-typewriter.test.ts`** (new) — jsdom, fake timers, 6 tests. Uses a properly typed factory (no casts):\n```ts\nfunction mediaQueryList(query: string, matches: boolean): MediaQueryList { … }\nwindow.matchMedia = (query: string) => mediaQueryList(query, query.includes(\"prefers-reduced-motion\") && reducedMotion);\n```\n\n**Row components** (`chat-item.tsx`, `project-list-sidebar/index.tsx`, `app-sidebar/app-sidebar-pinned.tsx`) — all now flex lines with in-flow actions:\n```tsx\n<SidebarMenuItem className={cn(\n  \"flex items-center rounded-md pr-1 hover:bg-sidebar-accent has-[a:focus-visible]:inset-ring-2 has-[a:focus-visible]:inset-ring-sidebar-ring\",\n  isActive && \"bg-sidebar-accent\")}>\n  <SidebarMenuButton className=\"h-auto min-w-0 flex-1 py-1.5 hover:bg-transparent focus-visible:ring-0 active:bg-transparent data-active:bg-transparent\" … />\n  <HoverReveal atRest={isPinned}><Tooltip><TooltipTrigger render={<SidebarRowAction onClick={togglePin} />}>…</TooltipTrigger>…</Tooltip></HoverReveal>\n  <DropdownMenu …><HoverReveal atRest={isActive}><DropdownMenuTrigger render={<SidebarRowAction />}>…</DropdownMenuTrigger></HoverReveal>…</DropdownMenu>\n</SidebarMenuItem>\n```\nPinned rail uses `has-data-active:bg-sidebar-accent` (parent can't see `isActive`) and `useOptionalActiveRuns`.\n\n**`apps/web/contexts/active-runs-context.tsx`** — added `useOptionalActiveRuns()` returning `ActiveRunsContextValue | null`, because `(admin)/admin/layout.tsx` mounts `AppSidebar` without `ActiveRunsProvider`.\n\n**`apps/web/contexts/__mocks__/active-runs-context.tsx`** — added `useOptionalActiveRuns = fn(() => useActiveRuns())`; missing exports here fail only `storybook build` (Vercel check), not dev/typecheck/lint/tests.\n\n**`packages/ui/src/styles/globals.css`** — `@property --marquee-fade-r`, `:root { --marquee-fade-max: 24px; }`, `@keyframes marquee-tail { from { --marquee-fade-r: var(--marquee-fade-max) } to { --marquee-fade-r: 0px } }`.\n\n**`packages/ui/src/components/input-group.tsx` + `.stories.tsx`** (new, vendored manually with JSDoc; 9 stories incl. 4 alignment examples added on review). `.oxlintrc.json` vendored-primitives override extended with `input-group.tsx` + `click-events-have-key-events`, `no-noninteractive-element-interactions`.\n\n**`apps/web/components/search-filter-input.tsx`** — rebuilt on `InputGroup`/`InputGroupAddon`/`InputGroupInput`/`InputGroupButton`.\n\n**`DESIGN.md`** §3 \"Overflow: fade and ellipsis mean different things\" — metric table now describes layout-based reserve, shimmer and retype rates; four rules including \"Only the edge that can be reached gets a fade\".\n\n**design-sync files:**\n- `.design-sync/config.json`: `projectId 0f7e4a36-9f43-4c15-be85-dbf5912a88c9`, `shape storybook`, `pkg @workspace/ui`, `globalName LlameDesignSystem0f7e4a`, `entry .design-sync/entry.ts`, `storybookConfigDir apps/storybook/.storybook`, `storybookStatic .design-sync/sb-reference`, 40 titleMap mappings + 19 `null` exclusions, `overrides` = `Message.skip` (markdown, math-delimiters), `Button.cardMode column`, `ScrollArea.cardMode column`, `Sidebar.cardMode single/primaryStory Basic`.\n- `.design-sync/entry.ts` — generated barrel, 43 modules, excludes 7 heavy ones, special-cases `ai-elements/shimmer` (`export { Shimmer }` only, `TextShimmerProps` collides).\n- `.design-sync/package.json` — `{\"name\":\"@workspace/ui\",\"types\":\"./entry.ts\"}` so the converter finds a type surface.\n- `.design-sync/previews/{Message,Conversation}.tsx` — hand-authored, plain strings instead of `MessageResponse`.\n- `.design-sync/NOTES.md` — full findings, exclusions, re-sync risks.\n- `.gitignore` — added `.design-sync/sb-reference/`, `learnings/`, `.cache/`, `node_modules`, `.ds-sync/`, `ds-bundle/`.\n\n**Memories written:** `~/.claude/projects/-home-leon0399-Projects-llame/memory/no-double-casts-in-new-code.md` (new) and an added \"Third gotcha\" section in `storybook-apps-web-sbmock-instance.md`.\n\n## 4. Errors and Fixes\n\n1. **Tailwind template-literal classes** — first version used `${px(...)}` interpolation; Tailwind's extractor is lexical, so rewrote with literal class strings.\n2. **`calc(100%-24px)` invalid** — needs `calc(100%_-_24px)` (underscores become spaces).\n3. **Excerpt faded instead of ellipsed / badge cut / clearance too big** (user screenshots) — abandoned the mask-on-column approach for hover padding, later for in-flow layout.\n4. **Band case (title fits at rest, clipped on hover)** — measured mid-transition geometry; fixed with always-on `ResizeObserver` + separate `data-overflowing`/`data-c