e animation? and the marque is broken, it isn't scrolled when text fits pre-hover and doesnt fit post-hover\"\n5. \"the right/end fade disappeares the moment scrolling starts, it should only disapper when scolling stops\"\n6. \"There is still no right-/end-side fade: (see 2000 being cut)\"\n7. \"The problem is that your fade starts the removal transition with the scroll animation start, regardless of the text width/length, but it should end with scroll\"\n8. \"/code-review --fix\"\n9. \"/simplify; and wait for all results of code-review and simplifier before acting\"\n10. \"after sweeping - open a PR and monitor reviews\"\n11. \"Can you braintorm and analyze if the start / left fade when marque animation starts really required, because now I look at it and it looks weird. What would be better - leave it or remove it?\"\n12. \"ok, let's drop it then\"\n13. \"are you sure that const-style reusable classes is correct approach here? Wouldn't they be skipped by Tailwind compiler to optimize production build? Wouldn't something like class-variance-authority be better here? Anyways this seems incorrect, I do not like it, we should use some true react-style decorators or wrapper classes may be, or some hooks/helpers\"\n14. \"also, I believe the pinned main-rail titles should also receive the fade + no-reserved-space-for-invisible-buttons treatment as well\"\n15. \"let's do a short spec if needed, but we are not going to include it in the commit, PR stays implementation-only\"\n16. **\"wait, the `x as unknown as T` pattern is banned for new code, do not use it, do proper typing, not cheating\"**\n17. \"Also, I think I do not like that hardcoded `pr-13` approach in general, it is hardcoded to the specific button sizes and count, I think it should be dynamic - just a div with `display: none` unless parent hovered, and margin with fade or smth similar with hooks, not sure, just more universal, that does not depend on number of icons and their size, something that we may adapt for other cases, even without buttons at all (just hover-marque) or something that is different than buttons\"\n18. \"Wait, I just realized, is this issue in the vendored components or our bespoke ones?\"\n19. \"yes, fold into #324, app-code only, primitive untouched\"\n20. \"Stop, it is broken: 1) buttons / icons are small, I want it to be 1-to-1 the same as it was 2) the container for the list-item is shrinking on hover, it should stay the same full-width\"\n21. \"can we along the way fix that these list-items are not focusable / accesible themselves? I cannot tab through them -> hit enter and open the chat / project\"\n22. \"continue from where you left off. I still cannot tab over items themselves, only action buttons\"\n23. \"that's weird, my tab-pressing order is the following: - collapse sidebar - search (skips 'new chat') - kebab for pinned chat - kebab for pinned project - profile (skips 'administration') (second list sidebar with chats) - pin button for chat (skipped 'new chat' in the heading) - kebab button for the same chat … and so on\"\n24. \"I'm using chromium-based Vivaldi\"\n25. \"dinally, got it working. Now, fix that the focus ring is truncated at the top by the grouping header\"\n26. \"One more bug with collapsed pinned rail items: on the active item kebab menu is still visible, leading to the weird truncated view of the chat icon and kebab button\"\n27. `/design-login`, then `/design-sync`\n28. \"wait, there is already an existing Claude Design project\" (as: \"There is already an existing Claude Design project\")\n29. \"wait, does it sync current code/design to the Claude Design project or other way around and currently re-doing all our existing working UI? Or I'm not getting what this tool does?\"\n30. **\"btw, if the `.design-sync` is going to be commited, make sure it is done in a separate stacked PR on the current one, as per /gh-stack\"**\n\n## 7. Pending Tasks\n\n- Finish the design-sync verification campaign: grade the remaining 5 components (Command, Conversation, Message, ModelSwitchBoundary, Select) — wave-2 agents `ds-fixups` (Switch/Toggle/ToggleGroup/Form) and `ds-ai` (Message/Conversation/ModelSwitchBoundary) plus `ds-overlays` are running.\n- Fold all `.design-sync/learnings/*.md` into `NOTES.md` and delete them (a full compare prints `[LEARNINGS_UNMERGED]` and the driver fails its verdict while they exist).\n- Apply any config skips (e.g. `Form` validation stories if genuinely unreproducible) in one batched full rebuild + validate.\n- Author `.design-sync/conventions.md`, set `readmeHeader`, then re-run the driver (`resync.mjs` without `--remote`) as the §4d closing receipt.\n- Atomic upload to project `0f7e4a36-9f43-4c15-be85-dbf5912a88c9`: `finalize_plan` with full writes + reviewed deletes (no anchor exists), sentinel → content → deletes → sentinel re-arm → `_ds_sync.json` last.\n- Decide whether to add `SKILL.md` to the upload plan (it documents the now-dead global `window.LlameDesignSystem_0f7e4a`; emitted global is `LlameDesignSystem0f7e4a`).\n- Commit `.design-sync/` **as a separate stacked PR on #324 via the `/gh-stack` skill**.\n- PR #324: user still needs to re-approve the `__screenshots__` visual baselines (storyproof can only capture/approve from the dev Storybook panel).\n\n## 8. Current Work\n\nImmediately before this summary I was orchestrating the design-sync verification campaign (skill §4c fan-out). State at last check:\n\n```\ngraded: 35/40\nungraded: Command Conversation Message ModelSwitchBoundary Select\nlearnings: feedback.md forms.md layout.md solo.md\n```\n\nBatch results so far: solo (Button, Avatar, Dialog) — Button 6/6 match, Avatar 6/6 match (remote-image canary CLEAR), Dialog 3 match + 2 mismatch; forms (9) — 7 match, 5 stories deferred; feedback (9) — 9/9 match, Kbd `close`; layout (8) — 8/8 match with owned previews for Accordion/Collapsible/Tabs/Sidebar. `ds-overlays` (AlertDialog, Sheet, Popover, DropdownMenu, HoverCard, Tooltip, Select, Command) has written 8 owned previews and been asked for its final report but has not yet replied.\n\nThe campaign's central finding, confirmed by three independent batches: **compiled previews never run a story's `play` function**, so Storybook's reference is captured post-interaction while the preview renders the pre-interaction state; the fix is to seed the story's computed end state as a prop (`defaultOpen`/`defaultChecked`/`defaultValue`/`useState` seed) in an owned `.tsx`, read from the play function's full sequence. Also twice-confirmed: `compare.mjs` intermittently reports one component as all-`unpaired`/0-cells inside a multi-component batch run, and a scoped re-run of that component alone captures cleanly (retry once).\n\nPR #324 is at 11 commits, last being `6b39089a` (\"fix(web): drop row actions in the icon-collapsed rail\"), CI green on the prior head, `MERGEABLE`.\n\n## 9. Optional Next Step\n\nWait for `ds-overlays`, `ds-fixups` and `ds-ai` to report, then perform the mandatory between-waves fold: \"Read every `.design-sync/learnings/*.md`. Promote `[GENERAL]` bullets into `.design-sync/NOTES.md` (dedup; keep them terse), then delete each learnings file you've folded\" — and apply any config edits the subagents requested (skip lists / `cardMode`) in one batched full rebuild + validate, since I told the user: \"I'll batch every such story from all four batches into one config edit once the wave finishes, rather than paying a rebuild per discovery.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/leon0399/.claude/projects/-home-leon0399--herdr-worktrees-llame-redesign-chat-list-hover-action/e6563ef5-8cc9-4868-80e4-04eb84a83133.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. P