ampling rule — exhaustively for these, since every one of yours is an overlay/portal component; diagnose failures via the decision tree.\n2. Copy .design-sync/.cache/previews/<Name>.tsx to .design-sync/previews/<Name>.tsx and DELETE its first-line `// @ds-preview generated …` marker. Mirror the story's JSX; inline story-local fixture data.\n3. node .ds-sync/lib/preview-rebuild.mjs --config .design-sync/config.json --node-modules packages/ui/node_modules --out ./ds-bundle --components <Name>\n4. node .ds-sync/storybook/compare.mjs --out ./ds-bundle --storybook-static .design-sync/sb-reference --components <Name>\n5. Re-Read the fresh sheet and Write verdicts to .design-sync/.cache/compare/<Name>.grade.json ({\"stories\": {\"<story>\": {\"verdict\": \"match|close|mismatch\", \"note\": \"…\"}}}). Done when every story grades match. A close story is still a fix target — accept close only when an iteration didn't improve it, and the note must say what's off AND what you tried.\n\nTHE KNOWN ISSUE FOR YOUR BATCH (found in the solo phase — expect it everywhere):\nOverlay stories that storybook opens via a play function render CLOSED in previews (previews compose the story but never run play). Storybook shows the open panel; the preview shows only the trigger. The fix is an owned .tsx forcing the open state (`defaultOpen` / `open`), which for portal components usually pairs with cfg.overrides.<Name>.cardMode \"single\" — that config edit is NOT yours to make: record it in your learnings file and final report, and the orchestrator applies it.\n\nHARD RULES — violating these corrupts other agents' work:\n- Edit ONLY .design-sync/previews/<your components>.tsx, your components' .design-sync/.cache/compare/*.grade.json, and .design-sync/learnings/overlays.md.\n- NEVER edit .design-sync/config.json, .design-sync/NOTES.md, .ds-sync/, or any other component's files.\n- NEVER run package-build.mjs or package-validate.mjs — they rewrite the shared bundle. preview-rebuild.mjs + compare.mjs scoped via --components are your only build commands.\n- NEVER write an image-judged grade for images you haven't Read in this iteration.\n- NEVER \"fix\" overlay bleed by neutralizing a story's open state in the .tsx — that destroys the fidelity being verified.\n- If the SAME root cause appears in 2+ of your components — or once when it is config-level — STOP on those, write it to your learnings file prefixed [GENERAL], report it, and do not work around it per-component.\n\nLearnings: append to .design-sync/learnings/overlays.md as you go — one bullet per discovery: `<Component>: <symptom> → <root cause> → <fix>`, prefixed [GENERAL] if it applies beyond that component.\n\nKnown repo gotchas (read before starting):\n- `@workspace/ui` ships source with wildcard subpath exports and no dist. The bundle is built from a barrel at .design-sync/entry.ts. Owned previews import components with the BARE package specifier, e.g. `import { Dialog } from \"@workspace/ui/components/dialog\"` — that resolves only because packages/ui/node_modules/@workspace/ui is symlinked to packages/ui. Do not use relative paths into packages/ui.\n- Framing differs by design: storybook crops tight to the component, previews render on a full page, and storybook captures can carry a focus ring. Both are ignorable per the rubric — judge the component, not the canvas.\n- The remote-image canary is CLEAR (Avatar's shadcn.png loads on both panels), so missing images in YOUR sheets would be a real defect, not a sandbox artifact.\n- Markdown/code rendering is deliberately absent from the bundle (Shiki's grammars are 14.6 MB against a 12 MB cap), so nothing in your batch should import MessageResponse or ReasoningContent.\n\nFinal report: per component — match/close/blocked + one-line reason; then any [GENERAL] learnings verbatim.\n</teammate-message>",
