            "content": "# Overlay/portal batch learnings (AlertDialog, Sheet, Popover, DropdownMenu, HoverCard, Tooltip, Select, Command)\n\n- [GENERAL] **The storybook reference screenshot is an element screenshot bound to `#storybook-root`'s bounding box** (`compare.mjs`: `el = await sbPage.$(SB_ROOT); png = await el.screenshot(SHOT)`), not a full-page capture. Radix/Base UI overlay content (`DropdownMenuContent`, `SelectContent`, `TooltipContent`, popper-anchored `PopoverContent`, `HoverCardContent`) portals to `document.body`, outside that root element's DOM subtree — Playwright's `elementHandle.screenshot()` crops to the element's *current page position/size*, so it only shows overlay content that visually overlaps that small rect. Concretely: DropdownMenu/Select/Tooltip/HoverCard triggers keep a tiny (~90×60px) bbox even when their popper-positioned content opens below/beside them (no overlap → reference shows only the closed trigger), while centered content (AlertDialog, Sheet, Command's `CommandDialog`, a Popover nested in an open Dialog) visually overlaps the same page region the trigger sits in (both centered), so the reference legitimately shows a slice of the open content. **This is a capture-mechanism artifact, not evidence the component failed to open** — grade per SKILL.md §4's \"reference side is the artifact\" rule: verify the pixels *inside* the reference's frame match (they should, since it's the same page state), and that the preview mirrors the story JSX/end-state verbatim; don't downgrade a portal story just because its reference thumbnail looks like a closed trigger.\n- [GENERAL] **The fix is \"mirror the story's final rendered state,\" not \"force every overlay open.\"** Stories whose `play` dismisses the overlay before ending (most `Small`/`Media`/`Checkboxes`/`RadioGroup`-style variants across every component in this batch) render correctly with an unforced, plain render — storybook's own screenshot shows them closed too. Only stories whose